@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Cookie Policy & Local Storage Transparency";
}

<section class="legal-page">
    <div class="container container-narrow">
        <div class="legal-header">
            <div class="hero-tag">
                <span class="badge-tag badge-green">🍪 Storage Transparency</span>
            </div>
            <h1 class="legal-title">Cookie &amp; Local Storage Policy</h1>
            <div class="legal-meta">
                <span>Compliance: ePrivacy Directive &bull; GDPR &bull; CCPA</span>
                <span>Last Updated: August 31, 2026</span>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="legal-content">
            <div class="highlight-box">
                <strong>Zero Tracking Cookies:</strong> Stream Helper does not use tracking cookies, advertising beacons, or third-party behavioral analytics cookies of any kind.
            </div>

            <h2>1. What Are Cookies and Local Storage?</h2>
            <p>Cookies and client-side storage technologies (such as <code>localStorage</code>, <code>chrome.storage.local</code>, and <code>IndexedDB</code>) are small data files stored locally on your device by your web browser to remember user preferences and state across sessions.</p>

            <h2>2. How Stream Helper Uses Local Storage</h2>
            <p>We utilize strictly necessary client-side storage mechanisms exclusively for core application functionality:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>User Interface Preferences:</strong> Remembering your chosen parallel thread count (e.g. 16, 32, 64 workers), theme preferences, and default file-naming structures.</li>
                <li><strong>Temporary Task Buffer:</strong> Caching active segment progress during a download session so that network interruptions can resume without data loss.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>3. Zero Marketing or Analytics Cookies</h2>
            <p>Our website and browser extension contain:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>❌ No Google Analytics or advertising tracking tags</li>
                <li>❌ No cross-site social media tracking pixels</li>
                <li>❌ No third-party data sharing or affiliate beacons</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>4. Managing and Clearing Local Storage</h2>
            <p>You have full control over all stored data. You can clear your browser's local storage and extension data at any time through your browser settings:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Chrome / Edge / Brave:</strong> Settings &rarr; Privacy &amp; Security &rarr; Clear Browsing Data &rarr; Cookies and other site data.</li>
                <li><strong>Extension Data:</strong> Right-click the Stream Helper extension icon &rarr; Manage Extension &rarr; Clear Storage.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
